1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,511
The matrix a science fiction film created by the wkis is probably one of the most influential movies ever made.
作者认为，科幻片《黑客帝国》可能是有史以来影响最大的电影之一；创作者姓名字幕 wkis 待核。

2
00:00:07,521 --> 00:00:16,990
The story starts when computer programmer thomas anderson operating as a hacker under the alias neo discovers the truth about the world he's living in.
故事从电脑程序员 Thomas Anderson 开始：他用 Neo 的化名当黑客，发现自己生活的世界的真相。

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,920
As he becomes aware of the existence of something known as the matrix.
他逐渐意识到，有某种叫作 Matrix 的东西存在。

4
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:28,830
After looking for a man named morphus who can tell him more about the matrix he encounters another hacker named trinity.
他寻找一个叫 Morphus 的人，希望了解更多，然后遇到另一名叫 Trinity 的黑客。

5
00:00:28,840 --> 00:00:35,601
After a failed attack which led to agent smith capturing and bugging him trinity takes neo to morpheus.
一次失败的袭击导致 Smith 探员抓住他并安装窃听装置，随后 Trinity 带 Neo 去见 Morpheus。

6
00:00:35,601 --> 00:00:45,761
Morpheus vaguely describes the matrix as this all encompassing prison as the world that has been pulled over neo's eyes blinding him from the truth.
Morpheus 含糊地把 Matrix 描述成无所不包的监狱，是蒙住 Neo 双眼、让他看不见真相的世界。

7
00:00:45,761 --> 00:00:50,200
He also admits that no one can be told what the matrix is.
他还承认，没有人能直接被告知 Matrix 究竟是什么。

8
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:53,281
You have to see it for yourself he states.
“你必须亲眼看看，”他说。

9
00:00:53,281 --> 00:00:59,801
So neo gets offered a choice in the form of two pills a blue one and a red one.
于是 Neo 面前出现一个选择，以两颗药丸的形式呈现：一颗蓝色、一颗红色。

10
00:00:59,801 --> 00:01:05,991
If he chooses the blue pill he remains in his everyday life and believes whatever he wants to believe.
选蓝药丸，他就留在日常生活中，继续相信自己想相信的事情。

11
00:01:06,001 --> 00:01:13,920
But if he chooses the red pill he'll set foot in the real world and find out what the matrix truly is.
选红药丸，他会踏入真实世界，发现 Matrix 真正是什么。

12
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:23,600
All I'm offering is the truth says morpheus and so neo takes the red pill and tumbles down the rabbit hole.
Morpheus 说“我提供的只有真相”。于是 Neo 吃下红药丸，跌进兔子洞。

13
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:36,880
The matrix is considered a philosophical film that contains many existing philosophical and religious themes like prophecy love truth karma the nature of reality and living in a simulation.
作者说，《黑客帝国》被视为哲学电影，包含预言、爱、真相、因果、现实本质和模拟生活等哲学与宗教主题。

14
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:43,270
But there seems to be a particular close connection between the matrix and plato's allegory of the cave.
但作者认为，它与柏拉图的洞穴寓言似乎有尤其紧密的联系。

15
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:52,200
In this allegory presented in plato's republic socrates describes a group of people chained to a wall within a cave their whole lives.
在《理想国》中的这则寓言里，苏格拉底描述了一群终生被锁在洞穴墙边的人。

16
00:01:52,200 --> 00:02:00,471
The only reality they know of is the mere shadows projected on the wall in front of them and they believe these are real entities.
他们所知的唯一现实，是眼前墙上投射出的影子，而他们相信这些是真实存在的东西。

17
00:02:00,481 --> 00:02:07,361
Then one of the prisoners is freed he leaves the cave and gets to experience the real world outside.
后来一个囚徒获得自由，离开洞穴，体验到外面的真实世界。

18
00:02:07,361 --> 00:02:14,120
But when he returns to the cave to enlighten the other prisoners with the truth he faces resistance.
但当他返回洞穴，想用真相启发其他囚徒时，却遭到抵抗。

19
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:19,521
This video analyzes the matrix film through the lens of plato's allegory of the cave.
本视频将透过柏拉图洞穴寓言来分析《黑客帝国》。

20
00:02:19,521 --> 00:02:38,481
While exploring the following question do we as human beings actually want the truth please note this video contains spoilers that reveal the plot.
同时探索：人类真的想要真相吗？请注意，本视频有揭示剧情的剧透。

21
00:02:38,481 --> 00:02:43,921
The prisoners of the cave are chained so that they cannot move their legs and necks.
洞穴里的囚徒被锁住，腿和脖子都无法移动。

22
00:02:43,921 --> 00:02:52,241
They can only sit and watch the wall in front of them but cannot look around cannot see each other nor the wall they're chain to.
他们只能坐着看面前的墙，不能环顾、看彼此，也看不到自己被锁着的那面墙。

23
00:02:52,241 --> 00:03:06,760
Behind the prisoners burns a fire there are people in between the fire and the prisoners these people hold sticks with several forms birds horses dogs which project onto the wall.
囚徒身后有火；火和囚徒之间有人举着带鸟、马、狗等形状的杆子，把影子投射在墙上。

24
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:14,600
So all they've ever seen are mere projections of objects that appear in the real world a world that's alien to them.
因此他们看到的只是现实中物体的投影，而那个世界对他们完全陌生。

25
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:23,081
When one of the prisoners is freed and ascends from the cave into the real world he experiences sunlight for the first time in his life.
当一个囚徒被释放，从洞穴升到真实世界时，他人生第一次看到了阳光。

26
00:03:23,081 --> 00:03:28,481
He is confused and needs time to adapt as he has never seen the daylight before.
他困惑不已，需要时间适应，因为他以前从没看过日光。

27
00:03:28,481 --> 00:03:36,801
But when his eyes have adjusted he encounters all the forms he recognizes from his life in the cave but they're different this time.
但眼睛适应后，他看到那些在洞穴生活中认得的形状，这一次却不同了。

28
00:03:36,801 --> 00:03:43,631
Instead of mere silhouettes he sees the actual entities full of color and with profound detail.
他看到的不再仅仅是轮廓，而是色彩丰富、细节充足的真实物体。

29
00:03:43,641 --> 00:03:48,201
He then realizes what he thought was real was in fact an illusion.
于是他意识到，自己原以为真实的东西，其实是幻象。
